-- emit: a primitive comparison in EVIDENCE position is a function, not an
-- operator (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §8.2, §9.1).
--
-- §8.3 turns `a < b` on an `Int` into `a < b`, because there is a concrete
-- pair to apply the operator to. An evidence slot has no such pair — it
-- wants a value of two arguments — so the module emits the comparator once
-- and hands its name over. That is the difference between the two sections,
-- and this fixture is where both are visible in one file.
--
-- Three of the four are emitted here, once each, sorted by printed name
-- text and placed ahead of every declaration (§8.5) — a module-level
-- constant's initialiser runs at load time and would otherwise read a
-- `const` that is still in its temporal dead zone. `String` is the fourth
-- and is NOT one of them: it routes to `core/String.beni`'s own `compare`,
-- imported like any other cross-module value, because `<` on JavaScript
-- strings is UTF-16 code-unit order and that function is Unicode scalar
-- order (A.26).
import Node exposing (Program)


before : a, a → Bool
    where a.compare : a, a → Order
before x y = x < y


sameAs : a, a → Bool
    where a.eq : a, a → Bool
sameAs x y = x == y


pub ints : Int, Int → Bool
ints a b = before a b


pub chars : Char, Char → Bool
chars a b = before a b


pub strings : String, String → Bool
strings a b = before a b


pub sameInts : Int, Int → Bool
sameInts a b = sameAs a b


main : Program
main = Node.printLines []
